 (superseded-record . "#hasheq((base-commit . \"54283f7f72124bf248b7883558aec71d21c992fc\") (branch . \"main\") (campaign . \"v1.00.24-test-design-hotspot-remediation\") (kind . \"wave-evidence\") (note . \"fixture-root runner discovery delivered: collect-test-files (scripts/run-tests/classify.rkt) and the downstream metadata selection helper (scripts/run-tests/classify-metadata.rkt) gained a #:root / #:test-root seam; an omitted root preserves the default repository discovery behavior, so production default collection, suite definitions, shard algorithm, scheduler, and CI invocation are unchanged. Unit assertions moved onto the hermetic fixture tree tests/fixtures/run-tests-discovery/ (fast, slow, platform, TUI, helper, malformed/edge metadata, nested, and symlink cases): tests/test-run-tests-shard.rkt is 35/35 @speed fast covering deterministic relative-path sort, metadata/heuristic selection, platform inclusion, shard partition, helper/fixture exclusion, missing-root failure, no escape through symlinks or .., and exit-code propagation of rackunit failures through the runner. Real repository-scale discovery is owned by the new L4 smoke tests/test-run-tests-repository-discovery.rkt (7/7, @speed slow, truthful integration/process metadata) asserting invariant properties (nonempty discovery, root containment, deterministic selected-path digests) instead of brittle live counts. Ledger docs/reports/TEST-RETIER-LEDGER-v1.00.24.rktd gained two W5 rows (RUNNER-DISCOVERY-UNIT-FIXTURE-ROOT unit-fast, RUNNER-REPOSITORY-DISCOVERY-L4 slow/L4) and the regenerated gate-ownership map checks clean (14 behaviors, 0 errors); the W0 fitness test tests/test-test-gate-ownership.rkt was updated to freeze all 14 behavior IDs — this was the root cause of the previously failed delivery verification. Hotspot after-manifest artifacts/test-runtime/v1.00.24-hotspots/w5-discovery-after.json holds 10 post-change samples for tests/test-run-tests-shard.rkt (all pass, median 930ms, min 904, max 951